{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>But if you remember me when it is well with you</b> — If you remember me, when it goes well with you, do now kindness and truth with me, and mention me to Pharaoh. And if the expression is one of request: \"But if you remember me and do kindness — kindness with me you shall mention me to Pharaoh.\" The meaning of \"with you\" is that you should remember me to do good with me when it goes well with you that you have gone out from the prison house. Or its meaning may be: that you should remember me in your heart as though I were with you. And the mentioning to Pharaoh is that he should praise him to him, saying, \"Behold, in the house of the chief executioner's servant there is a fine servant; he may stand before kings.\" And what also seems correct in my eyes is that he says: If you remember me to be with you when it goes well with you, and you return to your rank and desire to do this kindness with me, mention me to Pharaoh, saying in his presence, \"I remembered a youth who served me in the prison house; give him to me to be my attendant,\" and you will bring me out of this house, for it is a great sin upon those who keep me here. Or the meaning of \"and you shall mention me to Pharaoh\" may be: For Pharaoh saw me when I was a servant to his officer and overseer over all that was his, serving before him, and if you mention me before him, you will bring me out from here, for there is no iniquity in me that I have sinned, and it is fitting for the king to bring me out and deliver me from the hand of my oppressors, for nothing is hidden from the king if he desires.\""], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:22:17.618306053Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}